deplete choline do we see a difference

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.520
in cells ability to grow in culture

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:53.760
conditions. In normal conditions these

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:55.919
cells grow completely fine. And if you

00:21:55.919 --> 00:21:57.280
think about it I just told you choline

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:58.720
is super important. So how is that the

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:02.720
case? So we used um that&#x27;s a question.

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:04.320
So how does cell sustain choline

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:06.240
metabolism and proliferate without

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:07.919
FODV1?

00:22:07.919 --> 00:22:10.559
And we use crisper based genetic screens

00:22:10.559 --> 00:22:13.440
to uncover some possible ways that the

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:14.880
cells are using to cope this. And this

00:22:14.880 --> 00:22:17.039
is a technically a little challenging

00:22:17.039 --> 00:22:19.120
but conceptually very simple. You take

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:21.280
cells with and without your gene of

00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:22.799
interest

00:22:22.799 --> 00:22:24.960
and then you just grow them and we use

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:27.520
this pool genetic crisper system that

00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:29.200
each cell has a different gene knocked

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:31.039
out in it. And then over time in a

00:22:31.039 --> 00:22:33.280
poolled fashion you ask if that gene

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:35.360
that got knocked out is essential for

00:22:35.360 --> 00:22:38.559
cells in your condition not having FOBR1

00:22:38.559 --> 00:22:40.640
for example to grow then at the end of

00:22:40.640 --> 00:22:42.720
your experiment you should see that

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:44.640
